  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Evaluate $\\sqrt[3]{8t+6}$ at $t=6.$",
  "worked_solution": "We replace $t$ with $6$ in the given expression, and simplify as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{8t+6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{8(6)+6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{48+6} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{54} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{27\\cdot 2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{27}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{3}^{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{2} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt[3]{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
